In the beginning God created the heavens:
Speak to the children of Israel, that they bring Me an offering. From everyone who gives it willingly with his heart you shall take My offering.
OT	And this is the offering which you shall take from them: gold, silver, and bronze;
OT	blue, purple, and scarlet thread, fine linen, and goats' hair;
OT	ram skins dyed red, badger skins, and acacia wood;
OT	oil for the light, and spices for the anointing oil and for the sweet incense;
OT	onyx stones, and stones to be set in the ephod and in the breastplate.
OT	And let them make Me a sanctuary, that I may dwell among them.
OT	According to all that I show you, that is, the pattern of the tabernacle and the pattern of all its furnishings, just so you shall make it.
OT	And they shall make an ark of acacia wood; two and a half cubits shall be its length, a cubit and a half its width, and a cubit and a half its height.

Take from among you an offering to the LORD. Whoever is of a willing heart, let him bring it as an offering to the LORD: gold, silver, and bronze;
OT	ram skins dyed red, badger skins, and acacia wood;
OT	onyx stones, and stones to be set in the ephod and in the breastplate.
OT	All who are gifted artisans among you shall come and make all that the LORD has commanded:

Then he shall offer from the sacrifice of the peace offering, as an offering made by fire to the LORD, its fat and the whole fat tail which he shall remove close to the backbone. And the fat that covers the entrails and all the fat that is on the entrails,
OT	the two kidneys and the fat that is on them by the flanks, and the fatty lobe attached to the liver above the kidneys, he shall remove;
OT	And if his offering is a goat, then he shall offer it before the LORD.

Only the tribe of Levi you shall not number, nor take a census of them among the children of Israel;
OT	but you shall appoint the Levites over the tabernacle of the Testimony, over all its furnishings, and over all things that belong to it; they shall carry the tabernacle and all its furnishings; they shall attend to it and camp around the tabernacle.
OT	And when the tabernacle is to go forward, the Levites shall take it down; and when the tabernacle is to be set up, the Levites shall set it up. The outsider who comes near shall be put to death.
OT	The children of Israel shall pitch their tents, everyone by his own camp, everyone by his own standard, according to their armies;
OT	but the Levites shall camp around the tabernacle of the Testimony, that there may be no wrath on the congregation of the children of Israel; and the Levites shall keep charge of the tabernacle of the Testimony.

The LORD bless you and keep you;
OT	The LORD make His face shine upon you, And be gracious to you;
OT	The LORD lift up His countenance upon you, And give you peace.'

This is what pertains to the Levites: From twenty-five years old and above one may enter to perform service in the work of the tabernacle of meeting;
OT	and at the age of fifty years they must cease performing this work, and shall work no more.
OT	They may minister with their brethren in the tabernacle of meeting, to attend to needs, but they themselves shall do no work. Thus you shall do to the Levites regarding their duties.

Aaron shall be gathered to his people, for he shall not enter the land which I have given to the children of Israel, because you rebelled against My word at the water of Meribah.
OT	Take Aaron and Eleazar his son, and bring them up to Mount Hor;
OT	and strip Aaron of his garments and put them on Eleazar his son; for Aaron shall be gathered to his people and die there.

And on the Sabbath day two lambs in their first year, without blemish, and two-tenths of an ephah of fine flour as a grain offering, mixed with oil, with its drink offering--
OT	this is the burnt offering for every Sabbath, besides the regular burnt offering with its drink offering.
OT	At the beginnings of your months you shall present a burnt offering to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, and seven lambs in their first year, without blemish;

And in the seventh month, on the first day of the month, you shall have a holy convocation. You shall do no customary work. For you it is a day of blowing the trumpets.
OT	You shall offer a burnt offering as a sweet aroma to the LORD: one young bull, one ram, and seven lambs in their first year, without blemish.
OT	and one-tenth for each of the seven lambs;
OT	also one kid of the goats as a sin offering, to make atonement for you;
OT	besides the burnt offering with its grain offering for the New Moon, the regular burnt offering with its grain offering, and their drink offerings, according to their ordinance, as a sweet aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD.
OT	On the tenth day of this seventh month you shall have a holy convocation. You shall afflict your souls; you shall not do any work.

Count up the plunder that was taken--of man and beast--you and Eleazar the priest and the chief fathers of the congregation;
OT	and divide the plunder into two parts, between those who took part in the war, who went out to battle, and all the congregation.
OT	And levy a tribute for the LORD on the men of war who went out to battle: one of every five hundred of the persons, the cattle, the donkeys, and the sheep;
