LORD, when You went out from Seir, When You marched from the field of Edom, The earth trembled and the heavens poured, The clouds also poured water;
OT	The mountains gushed before the LORD, This Sinai, before the LORD God of Israel.
OT	In the days of Shamgar, son of Anath, In the days of Jael, The highways were deserted, And the travelers walked along the byways.

I go the way of all the earth; be strong, therefore, and prove yourself a man.
OT	And keep the charge of the LORD your God: to walk in His ways, to keep His statutes, His commandments, His judgments, and His testimonies, as it is written in the Law of Moses, that you may prosper in all that you do and wherever you turn;
OT	that the LORD may fulfill His word which He spoke concerning me, saying, If your sons take heed to their way, to walk before Me in truth with all their heart and with all their soul,' He said, "you shall not lack a man on the throne of Israel.'

When Your people go out to battle against their enemy, wherever You send them, and when they pray to the LORD toward the city which You have chosen and the temple which I have built for Your name,
OT	then hear in heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.
OT	yet when they come to themselves in the land where they were carried captive, and repent, and make supplication to You in the land of those who took them captive, saying, We have sinned and done wrong, we have committed wickedness';

Moreover, concerning a foreigner, who is not of Your people Israel, but has come from a far country for the sake of Your great name and Your mighty hand and Your outstretched arm, when they come and pray in this temple;
OT	then hear from heaven Your dwelling place, and do according to all for which the foreigner calls to You, that all peoples of the earth may know Your name and fear You, as do Your people Israel, and that they may know that this temple which I have built is called by Your name.
OT	When Your people go out to battle against their enemies, wherever You send them, and when they pray to You toward this city which You have chosen and the temple which I have built for Your name,

You are the LORD God, Who chose Abram, And brought him out of Ur of the Chaldeans, And gave him the name Abraham;
OT	You found his heart faithful before You, And made a covenant with him To give the land of the Canaanites, The Hittites, the Amorites, The Perizzites, the Jebusites, And the Girgashites--To give it to his descendants. You have performed Your words, For You are righteous.
OT	You saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt, And heard their cry by the Red Sea.

Truly I know it is so, But how can a man be righteous before God?
OT	If one wished to contend with Him, He could not answer Him one time out of a thousand.
OT	God is wise in heart and mighty in strength. Who has hardened himself against Him and prospered?
OT	He removes the mountains, and they do not know When He overturns them in His anger;
OT	He shakes the earth out of its place, And its pillars tremble;
OT	He commands the sun, and it does not rise; He seals off the stars;
OT	He alone spreads out the heavens, And treads on the waves of the sea;
OT	He made the Bear, Orion, and the Pleiades, And the chambers of the south;
OT	If He goes by me, I do not see Him; If He moves past, I do not perceive Him;
OT	If He takes away, who can hinder Him? Who can say to Him, What are You doing?'

If you would prepare your heart, And stretch out your hands toward Him;
OT	If iniquity were in your hand, and you put it far away, And would not let wickedness dwell in your tents;
OT	Then surely you could lift up your face without spot; Yes, you could be steadfast, and not fear;
OT	Because you would forget your misery, And remember it as waters that have passed away,
OT	And your life would be brighter than noonday. Though you were dark, you would be like the morning.
OT	And you would be secure, because there is hope; Yes, you would dig around you, and take your rest in safety.
OT	You would also lie down, and no one would make you afraid; Yes, many would court your favor.
OT	But the eyes of the wicked will fail, And they shall not escape, And their hope--loss of life!

But He is unique, and who can make Him change? And whatever His soul desires, that He does.
OT	For He performs what is appointed for me, And many such things are with Him.
OT	Therefore I am terrified at His presence; When I consider this, I am afraid of Him.
OT	For God made my heart weak, And the Almighty terrifies me;
OT	Some remove landmarks; They seize flocks violently and feed on them;

Oh, that I were as in months past, As in the days when God watched over me;
OT	When His lamp shone upon my head, And when by His light I walked through darkness;
OT	Just as I was in the days of my prime, When the friendly counsel of God was over my tent;
OT	When the Almighty was yet with me, When my children were around me;
OT	When my steps were bathed with cream, And the rock poured out rivers of oil for me!
OT	When I went out to the gate by the city, When I took my seat in the open square,

If I have kept the poor from their desire, Or caused the eyes of the widow to fail,
OT	Or eaten my morsel by myself, So that the fatherless could not eat of it
OT	(But from my youth I reared him as a father, And from my mother's womb I guided the widow );
OT	If I have seen anyone perish for lack of clothing, Or any poor man without covering;
OT	If his heart has not blessed me, And if he was not warmed with the fleece of my sheep;
OT	If I have raised my hand against the fatherless, When I saw I had help in the gate;
OT	If I have made gold my hope, Or said to fine gold, "You are my confidence';

If it had not been the LORD who was on our side, When men rose up against us,
OT	Then they would have swallowed us alive, When their wrath was kindled against us;
OT	Then the waters would have overwhelmed us, The stream would have gone over our soul;
OT	Then the swollen waters Would have gone over our soul.

Surely I will not go into the chamber of my house, Or go up to the comfort of my bed;
OT	I will not give sleep to my eyes Or slumber to my eyelids,
OT	Until I find a place for the LORD, A dwelling place for the Mighty One of Jacob.

As for the head of those who surround me, Let the evil of their lips cover them;
OT	Let burning coals fall upon them; Let them be cast into the fire, Into deep pits, that they rise not up again.
OT	Let not a slanderer be established in the earth; Let evil hunt the violent man to overthrow him.

The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon Me, Because the LORD has anointed Me To preach good tidings to the poor; He has sent Me to heal the brokenhearted, To proclaim liberty to the captives, And the opening of the prison to those who are bound;
OT	To proclaim the acceptable year of the LORD, And the day of vengeance of our God; To comfort all who mourn,
OT	To console those who mourn in Zion, To give them beauty for ashes, The oil of joy for mourning, The garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness; That they may be called trees of righteousness, The planting of the LORD, that He may be glorified.

In those days and at that time I will cause to grow up to David A Branch of righteousness; He shall execute judgment and righteousness in the earth.
OT	In those days Judah will be saved, And Jerusalem will dwell safely. And this is the name by which she will be called: THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS.'
OT	For thus says the LORD: "David shall never lack a man to sit on the throne of the house of Israel;

Moab is destroyed; Her little ones have caused a cry to be heard;
OT	For in the Ascent of Luhith they ascend with continual weeping; For in the descent of Horonaim the enemies have heard a cry of destruction.
OT	Flee, save your lives! And be like the juniper in the wilderness.

You are My battle-ax and weapons of war: For with you I will break the nation in pieces; With you I will destroy kingdoms;
OT	With you I will break in pieces the horse and its rider; With you I will break in pieces the chariot and its rider;
OT	With you also I will break in pieces man and woman; With you I will break in pieces old and young; With you I will break in pieces the young man and the maiden;
OT	With you also I will break in pieces the shepherd and his flock; With you I will break in pieces the farmer and his yoke of oxen; And with you I will break in pieces governors and rulers.
OT	And I will repay Babylon And all the inhabitants of Chaldea For all the evil they have done In Zion in your sight," says the LORD.

Behold, all souls are Mine; The soul of the father As well as the soul of the son is Mine; The soul who sins shall die.
OT	But if a man is just And does what is lawful and right;
OT	If he has not eaten on the mountains, Nor lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, Nor defiled his neighbor's wife, Nor approached a woman during her impurity;
OT	If he has not oppressed anyone, But has restored to the debtor his pledge; Has robbed no one by violence, But has given his bread to the hungry And covered the naked with clothing;
OT	If he has not exacted usury Nor taken any increase, But has withdrawn his hand from iniquity And executed true judgment between man and man;
OT	If he has walked in My statutes And kept My judgments faithfully--He is just; He shall surely live! Says the Lord GOD.

If he begets a son who is a robber Or a shedder of blood, Who does any of these things
OT	And does none of those duties, But has eaten on the mountains Or defiled his neighbor's wife;
OT	If he has oppressed the poor and needy, Robbed by violence, Not restored the pledge, Lifted his eyes to the idols, Or committed abomination;
OT	If he has exacted usury Or taken increase--Shall he then live? He shall not live! If he has done any of these abominations, He shall surely die; His blood shall be upon him.
OT	If, however, he begets a son Who sees all the sins which his father has done, And considers but does not do likewise;

I will make you pass under the rod, and I will bring you into the bond of the covenant;
OT	I will purge the rebels from among you, and those who transgress against Me; I will bring them out of the country where they dwell, but they shall not enter the land of Israel. Then you will know that I am the LORD.
OT	As for you, O house of Israel," thus says the Lord GOD: "Go, serve every one of you his idols--and hereafter--if you will not obey Me; but profane My holy name no more with your gifts and your idols.

And you, son of man--will it not be in the day when I take from them their stronghold, their joy and their glory, the desire of their eyes, and that on which they set their minds, their sons and their daughters:
OT	on that day one who escapes will come to you to let you hear it with your ears;
OT	on that day your mouth will be opened to him who has escaped; you shall speak and no longer be mute. Thus you will be a sign to them, and they shall know that I am the LORD.'

Now these are the names of the tribes: From the northern border along the road to Hethlon at the entrance of Hamath, to Hazar Enan, the border of Damascus northward, in the direction of Hamath, there shall be one section for Dan from its east to its west side;
OT	by the border of Dan, from the east side to the west, one section for Asher;
OT	by the border of Asher, from the east side to the west, one section for Naphtali;
OT	by the border of Naphtali, from the east side to the west, one section for Manasseh;
OT	by the border of Manasseh, from the east side to the west, one section for Ephraim;
OT	by the border of Ephraim, from the east side to the west, one section for Reuben;
OT	by the border of Reuben, from the east side to the west, one section for Judah;
OT	by the border of Judah, from the east side to the west, shall be the district which you shall set apart, twenty-five thousand cubits in width, and in length the same as one of the other portions, from the east side to the west, with the sanctuary in the center.
OT	The district that you shall set apart for the LORD shall be twenty-five thousand cubits in length and ten thousand in width.

The rest shall belong to the prince, on one side and on the other of the holy district and of the city's property, next to the twenty-five thousand cubits of the holy district as far as the eastern border, and westward next to the twenty-five thousand as far as the western border, adjacent to the tribal portions; it shall belong to the prince. It shall be the holy district, and the sanctuary of the temple shall be in the center.
OT	Moreover, apart from the possession of the Levites and the possession of the city which are in the midst of what belongs to the prince, the area between the border of Judah and the border of Benjamin shall belong to the prince.
OT	As for the rest of the tribes, from the east side to the west, Benjamin shall have one section;

These are the exits of the city. On the north side, measuring four thousand five hundred cubits
OT	on the east side, four thousand five hundred cubits, three gates: one gate for Joseph, one gate for Benjamin, and one gate for Dan;
OT	on the south side, measuring four thousand five hundred cubits, three gates: one gate for Simeon, one gate for Issachar, and one gate for Zebulun;
OT	on the west side, four thousand five hundred cubits with their three gates: one gate for Gad, one gate for Asher, and one gate for Naphtali.
OT	All the way around shall be eighteen thousand cubits; and the name of the city from that day shall be: THE LORD IS THERE.

Bring charges against your mother, bring charges; For she is not My wife, nor am I her Husband! Let her put away her harlotries from her sight, And her adulteries from between her breasts;
OT	Lest I strip her naked And expose her, as in the day she was born, And make her like a wilderness, And set her like a dry land, And slay her with thirst.
OT	I will not have mercy on her children, For they are the children of harlotry.

I will betroth you to Me forever; Yes, I will betroth you to Me In righteousness and justice, In lovingkindness and mercy;
OT	I will betroth you to Me in faithfulness, And you shall know the LORD.
OT	It shall come to pass in that day That I will answer," says the LORD; "I will answer the heavens, And they shall answer the earth.

How can I give you up, Ephraim? How can I hand you over, Israel? How can I make you like Admah? How can I set you like Zeboiim? My heart churns within Me; My sympathy is stirred.
OT	I will not execute the fierceness of My anger; I will not again destroy Ephraim. For I am God, and not man, The Holy One in your midst; And I will not come with terror.
OT	They shall walk after the LORD. He will roar like a lion. When He roars, Then His sons shall come trembling from the west;

Yet I am the LORD your God Ever since the land of Egypt, And you shall know no God but Me; For there is no savior besides Me.
OT	I knew you in the wilderness, In the land of great drought.
OT	So I will be to them like a lion; Like a leopard by the road I will lurk;

Though they dig into hell, From there My hand shall take them; Though they climb up to heaven, From there I will bring them down;
OT	And though they hide themselves on top of Carmel, From there I will search and take them; Though they hide from My sight at the bottom of the sea, From there I will command the serpent, and it shall bite them;
OT	The Lord GOD of hosts, He who touches the earth and it melts, And all who dwell there mourn; All of it shall swell like the River, And subside like the River of Egypt.
OT	He who builds His layers in the sky, And has founded His strata in the earth; Who calls for the waters of the sea, And pours them out on the face of the earth--The LORD is His name.
OT	Are you not like the people of Ethiopia to Me, O children of Israel?" says the LORD. "Did I not bring up Israel from the land of Egypt, The Philistines from Caphtor, And the Syrians from Kir?

I will stretch out My hand against Judah, And against all the inhabitants of Jerusalem. I will cut off every trace of Baal from this place, The names of the idolatrous priests with the pagan priests--
OT	Those who worship the host of heaven on the housetops; Those who worship and swear oaths by the LORD, But who also swear by Milcom;
OT	Those who have turned back from following the LORD, And have not sought the LORD, nor inquired of Him.

Receive the gift from the captives--from Heldai, Tobijah, and Jedaiah, who have come from Babylon--and go the same day and enter the house of Josiah the son of Zephaniah.
OT	Take the silver and gold, make an elaborate crown, and set it on the head of Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest.
OT	Then speak to him, saying, Thus says the LORD of hosts, saying: "Behold, the Man whose name is the BRANCH! From His place He shall branch out, And He shall build the temple of the LORD;

Assuredly, I say to you, all sins will be forgiven the sons of men, and whatever blasphemies they may utter;
